  "summary": "Danish furniture golden age: sculpted teak and oak, organic comfort, joinery perfection by Wegner, Juhl and Møller.",
  "description": "Kaare Klint's systematic approach at the Royal Danish Academy trained a generation — Wegner, Arne Jacobsen, Poul Kjærholm, Finn Juhl — who married cabinetmaker craft with industrial production. Rounded edges, floating seats, paper-knife profiles and cord-weave seats defined the look exported worldwide in the 1950s-60s. Collectors rediscovered it in the 1990s, feeding today's vintage market and Scandinavian revival.",
